Safety Risk Assessment Study of Shield Construction of
Water Conveyance Tunnels in Collapsible Loess Areas
Type of Degree: Professional Degree
Specialty: Industrial Engineering and Management
ABSTRACT
In recent years, the development of society has aggravated the shortage of water
resources. The implementation of long-distance cross-basin water diversion and transfer
projects can effectively solve the problem of uneven distribution of water resources. The
importance of tunnels is obvious because of their large number, high construction difficulty
and long period in the construction of water conservancy projects. Compared with ordinary
tunnels, water conveyance tunnels need to cross large mountain ranges and are
characterized by long lines and large depths, and the geological risks are difficult to be
fully predicted at the investigation stage. Compared with other regions, the stability of the
tunnel may be seriously affected by the wetting phenomenon of loess. Compared with
other construction methods, shield construction has higher risk and brings more challenges
to the construction. Therefore, all the links involved in shield construction must be
controlled in detail during the shield construction process, which helps to prevent major
safety accidents and ensure the smooth progress of the project. This study mainly focuses
on the safety risk evaluation of the shield construction phase of water conveyance tunnels
in collapsible loess areas, and the final research results contain:
(1) Establishing a safety risk evaluation index system for shield construction of water
conveyance tunnel in collapsible loess areas. Firstly, based on the basis and principles of
safety risk identification of water conveyance tunnel construction, the safety risk
identification process of water conveyance tunnel shield construction in collapsible loess
areas based on WBS-RBS method is established, and the list of risk factors is listed after
identifying the safety risk factors in the construction of water conveyance tunnel shield in
detail. Then the evaluation index screening model is established from the comprehensive
consideration of the contribution rate, sensitivity and independence of the evaluation
indexes, and the final risk evaluation index system is obtained.


