(2) Constructing a safety risk evaluation model for shield construction of water
conveyance tunnel in collapsible loess areas. Firstly, considering the complexity and fuzzy
characteristics of the construction risk of the shield method of water conveyance tunnel
construction in collapsible loess areas, the Grey-DEMATEL method is used to carry out
the comprehensive assignment of indicators. Then, the ISM method is used to clarify the
hierarchical attribution of each influencing factor, quantify and visualize the risk
influencing factors, and provide an intuitive and efficient method for analyzing the
influencing factors of the safety risk of the shield construction of water conveyance tunnel.
Finally, the two-dimensional cloud model is used to analyze the safety status of the
indicators from the dimensions of the probability of risk occurrence and the degree of loss,
and the evaluation level of safety risk is determined.
(3) Application of safety risk evaluation model for shield construction of water
conveyance tunnel in collapsible loess areas. Analyze the construction characteristics and
challenges of the X water conveyance tunnel of the second phase of the Diversion of Han
Jiwei Project, and then apply the risk evaluation model to it, and get a lower safety risk
level of the shield construction of the X water conveyance tunnel, which is acceptable after
rectification, and the conclusion is highly consistent with the actual construction situation,
which verifies the reasonableness of the evaluation model. Finally, In response to the risk
evaluation results, specific and targeted risk prevention and treatment measures are
proposed, with a view to providing reference for the construction of water conveyance
tunnels in similar areas.
